## SQ-HSC-89 | salt caves in the set biomes: raw rock salt shell (desert box of SQ-FCK-08)
@group A
@commands HNH-89: locate a salt cave, enter it
@pass generates in the set biomes; shell is raw rock salt block; logged for the further eval
@fails no cave, or a dissolving shell
@from batches/r1113/c3_b1.qb
> zq count {DS1-112} -45 {DS3-112} {DS1+111} 40 {DS3+111} salt:raw_rock_salt_block
waitlog \[zq\] count salt:raw_rock_salt_block: \d+ 900
> zq count {DS1-112} -45 {DS3-112} {DS1+111} 40 {DS3+111} minecraft:cave_air
waitlog \[zq\] count minecraft:cave_air: \d+ 900
> forceload remove {DS1-112} {DS3-112} {DS1+111} {DS3+111}
expect \[zq\] count salt:raw_rock_salt_block: [1-9]
look the box is desert (in #hearthandharvest:has_salt_caves); rarity 24 gives about 9 attempts in 225 chunks; raw rock salt > 0 with cave air: caves generated; "dissolving shell" (water eating the salt) needs a look in game: for the further eval, record the counts. Row group was A; caves need a normal world, so it runs here

